ated socket\\n`<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC root) and §4.2 tmux\\nbackend (lines 1403-1449), with §4.C (1082), §4.D (1220), and\\n§4.E (1309) as context, plus §4.3 (1458) and §4.4 for the Windows\\nand broker rules. All clause citations name the pinned file, never\\nthe network, never v0.5.0.\\n\\n## Finding-by-finding table (verdict -> change -> test that fails without it -> evidence)\\n\\n| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| P2-A broker-or-refuse pinned at the entry only for fixture shapes: zero admission (R09), admitted-without-generation (R10), decoy-only (R19) server shapes walk through; ProbeServer unarmed on every background test (R18 fallback guard invisible) | Three server-admission subtests added to `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` AND mirrored in `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`; shipped `N-broker-zero-admission` at the `CheckBrokerContact` server wiring (R09 shape; R10/R19 share the anchor); fail-if-called `ProbeServer` spy armed in every background-path `Acquire` test (23/23 mechanical census); shipped `D-background-fallback-foreground` (R18 shape); row-31/README sentence extended to both foreground dependencies | The three new miss-table subtests + the three broker-contact mirror subtests (R09/R10/R19 shapes redden both tables firsthand); every miss-table subtest reddens under D-background-fallback-foreground | `harness-pass1/N-broker-zero-admission.log`, `harness-pass1/D-background-fallback-foreground.log` (+ pass 2), `logs/R10-R19-anchor-share.log` (unshipped-shape replay: both shapes KILLED by the new tests through both tables) |\\n| P3-A absence classifier pinned at the entry for mode and containment only (ownership member walks through, R01) | New `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` (unix-only file, `effectiveUID` seam) asserting top-level `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime ownership` with no broker contact and both spies silent; shipped `N-absence-remap-ownership` (R01 shape); sibling rows `N-absence-remap-containment` (R02) and `N-absence-remap-invalid` so every classifier member carries a row | `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` (foreign-owned leaf maps to `capability_unavailable` under the mutant; the top-level assertion reddens) | `harness-pass1/N-absence-remap-ownership.log`, `N-absence-remap-containment.log`, `N-absence-remap-invalid.log` (+ pass 2) |\\n| P3-B censusable \\\"before\\\" that is false (malformed session creates the directory and probes before refusing, P01) | Session identity parses at the foreground entry before `EnsureRuntimeDir` and the probe; no-directory/no-probe assertions added to `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession`; shipped `N-session-entry` | `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession` (under the mutant the request creates the directory and probes before the spawn-site refusal, tripping the new assertions while the refusal code stays correct) | `harness-pass1/N-session-entry.log` (+ pass 2), `logs/pkg-tests-v.log` |\\n| Obs-1 comma root walks past the TMUX split (P02) | Row 23/B16 scope comma roots out of the TMUX member's encoding (faithful to tmux(1) itself) | — (bound/prose, no behavior) | `TRACEABILITY.md` rows 23/B16 |\\n| Obs-2 relative alias walks past the cleaned-string gate (P03) | B16 reads \\\"symlinked or relative alias\\\" | — (bound/prose, no behavior) | `TRACEABILITY.md` B16 |\\n| Obs-3 Spawn inert on the background path (P04) | B9 + row 31 state the inert field and why the shared-Dependencies fallback shape is realistic | — (design note; the D-background-fallback-foreground row measures the fallback) | `TRACEABILITY.md` B9, row 31 |\\n| Obs-5 input-reachable constructor-failure arm unpinned (P06) | New `TestAcquireBackgroundInvalidGenerationRefusesAfterProbe` (invalid-UTF-8 generation refuses after the broker probe) + shipped `N-details-constructor`; B15 names the commit-side leaf-`Stat` and `NewGuard` arms | The new test (under the mutant the miss reports a zero outcome with nil error) | `harness-pass1/N-details-constructor.log` (+ pass 2) |\\n| Obs-6 static-gate exits live in prose only | `static-gates.log` records every exit code | — (evidence hygiene) | `logs/static-gates.log` |\\n\\nKept untouched per the verdict: the dedicated-server rule per vector,\\nthe background broker-or-refuse wiring with the literal\\n`capability_unavailable` and typed details, the no-fallback rule along\\nthe caller/credential/platform axes, the landed-admission attestation\\ncomposition, the custody gates that held under attack (FIFO/symlink/\\nmode/UID/handle-mismatch refusals, the explicit `Fchmod`, the\\nreal-SIGKILL crash test), the determinism design (no real-tmux\\nwitness), and the `internal/traceability` boundary.\\n\\n## The instrument: gate × entry census (the rework brief's deliverable)\\n\\nThree rounds in a row produced the same finding class at a new site\\neach time (rev3 P2-C foreground admission data, rev4 P2-B\\nRequest.Name, rev5 P2-A broker-server wiring): the defect was the\\nmeasurement, not the code. This revision ships the instrument: for\\nevery gate in the package, every production entry that can reach it —\\n`Acquire` foreground, `Acquire` background, `EnsureRuntimeDir`,\\n`VerifyRuntimeDir`, `BuildArgv`, `SocketPath`, `ResolveSocket`,\\n`ObserveAmbient`, `CheckBrokerContact`, `CheckServerAttested`, and\\n`checkCreationAllowed` called directly — with exactly one of: a\\nnamed committed test driving the gate through that entry plus an\\nadmitting narrowing row killing through that test; `unreachable` with\\nthe structural reason; or a stated bound. The census is a table in\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6546,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1637,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
