{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ff3b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c620-a10f-77d2-842c-eaf24fab8e2e"},"sequence":7672,"recorded_at":1780531400015339,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0cdc816d-6145-48a9-a49c-390655512ae9","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0cdc816d-6145-48a9-a49c-390655512ae9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0cdc816d-6145-48a9-a49c-390655512ae9"},"call_id":"call_01a0c67c350d723da7c658333fc9bdee","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n(139 line(s) above)\n140|## Mutation battery\n141|\n142|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py`:\n143|73 narrowing rows KILLED, 2 supplementary additive rows KILLED\n144|(D-background-fallback and D-background-fallback-foreground, labeled),\n145|1 harmless control SURVIVED, on two full passes with identical verdicts\n146|and one raw log per plant per run. Row N-deps-foreground kills by\n147|panic: the admitted request calls the nil spawner and the panic fails\n148|the test. Rows N-verify-absence-detail (background leg),\n149|N-broker-empty-generation, and N-commit-eacces-as-exist kill by reroute\n150|to a neighboring refusal, disclosed in their row notes.\n151|N-absence-remap-widen kills through the top-level custody oracle:\n152|under the errors.As helper the row survives (the reviewer's R05),\n153|under the top-level assertion it kills. N-details-constructor kills by\n154|typed-nil: the swallowed constructor failure returns a typed-nil\n155|*axerror.Error inside a non-nil error interface where the test expects\n156|the invalid-arguments refusal, and the top-level type assertion\n157|reddens. N-session-entry kills\n158|through the no-directory/no-probe assertions while the refusal code\n159|stays correct (the spawn-site arm still refuses the admitted member).\n160|No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source\n161|text, and the harness executes the behavioral suite (bound B4). The\n162|reviewers' error-arm plants (stat-failure arms flipped to fail-open,\n163|the unreachable guard arm, the unopenable-root arm) are reported as\n164|error-arm rows under bound B15, never counted among the narrowing\n165|rows.\n166|\n167|## Gate × entry census\n168|\n169|Every gate in the package against every production entry that could\n170|reach it. Columns: AFG = Acquire foreground, ABG = Acquire\n171|background, ENS = EnsureRuntimeDir, VER = VerifyRuntimeDir, ARG =\n172|BuildArgv, SOCK = SocketPath, RES = ResolveSocket, OBS =\n173|ObserveAmbient, BRO = CheckBrokerContact, SRV = CheckServerAttested,\n174|CRE = checkCreationAllowed called directly. Each cell states exactly\n175|one of: M (measured — a named committed test drives the gate through\n176|that entry and a shipped admitting narrowing row kills through that\n177|test; multi-entry rows list every entry their killers cover, verified\n178|per entry from the raw logs), U1 (entry takes no input this gate\n179|decides over), U2 (entry never reaches this code, with the structural\n180|reason), U3 (shadowed — an upstream arm refuses every such input\n181|through this entry first), B (stated bound with the reason). 50 of\n182|264 cells measured, 4 bounds, 210 unreachable with reasons; every\n183|reachable non-bound cell is measured (50 of 54).\n184|\n185|| Gate (site) | AFG | ABG | ENS | VER | ARG | SOCK | RES | OBS | BRO | SRV | CRE |\n186||---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n187|| caller (acquire.go:149) | M TestAcquireRefusesUnknownCaller / N-caller-vocabulary | U2 unknown callers refuse pre-dispatch; admission always dispatches foreground | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U2 vocabulary enforced upstream in Acquire; direct callers pass post-gate values |\n188|| details (acquire.go:152) | M TestAcquireRefusesMissingRealmDetails foreground / N-details-generation, N-details-brokerstate, N-details-remediation | M TestAcquireRefusesMissingRealmDetails background / same 3 rows | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 |\n189|| render (acquire.go:289) | U2 foreground never renders the unavailable refusal | M TestAcquireBackgroundInvalidGenerationRefusesAfterProbe / N-details-constructor | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 |\n190|| dispatch (acquire.go:163) | M TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer / N-dispatch-foreground | M TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable / N-dispatch-background | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 |\n191|| plat (runtime.go:76) | M TestAcquireRefusesUnknownPlatform + TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform foreground / N-platform-wiring + N-platform-windows | M same tests background / same rows | M TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadPlatform + TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWindowsOnUnixHost / same rows | M TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesBadLexical + WindowsOnUnixHost verify leg / same rows | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 |\n192|| root (runtime.go:87) | M TestAcquireForegroundRefusesBadRoot / N-root-wiring (relative member; missing member asserted here, row-pinned via ABG/ENS/VER) | M TestAcquireBackgroundMissingRootRefusesInvalid / N-root-missing-classify (missing member; relative member row-pinned via AFG/ENS/VER) | M TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadRoots / N-root-wiring + N-root-missing-classify | M TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesBadLexical + TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesMissingRoot / same rows | U1 applies no root grammar to its directory input | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 |\n193|| name (runtime.go:110) | U2 name is not an Acquire input; entry always passes RuntimeDirName (see wiring) | U2 name is not an Acquire input; entry always passes RuntimeDirName (see wiring) | M TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadNames / N-containment-slash (nested member; 5 other members test-pinned) | M TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesBadLexical nested / N-containment-slash | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 |\n194|| guard (runtime.go:93) | B B15 guard refusal arm unreachable through the name grammar; fail-open plant survives by construction | B B15 same | B B15 same | B B15 same | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 |\n195|| wiring (acquire.go:155,183,228) | M TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath foreground / N-wiring-lexical + N-wiring-ensure (verify site not reached from AFG) | M TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath background / N-wiring-lexical + N-wiring-verify | U2 leaf is a parameter; fixed-leaf choice lives in Acquire | U2 leaf is a parameter; fixed-leaf choice lives in Acquire | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 |\n196|| override (socket.go:85) | M TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector foreground ×6 / N-override-env, -inherited, -default, -conventional, -tmpdir, -whitespace | M same background ×6 / same 6 rows | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | M TestResolveSocketRefusesEveryOverrideVector ×6 / same 6 rows | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 |\n197|| collision (socket.go:106) | M TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision foreground ×5 + UncleanSpelling + TMUXEnvRealEncoding foreground / N-collision ×5 + N-collision-unclean + N-collision-tmuxenv-encoding | M same background / same 7 rows | U1 | U1 | U2 compares the spawn socket under G-argv, not ambient members | U1 | M direct collision tables / same 7 rows | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 |\n198|| deps (acquire.go:180,222) | M TestAcquireRefusesMissingDependencies FG + TestAcquireForegroundNilSpawnWithProbeRefuses / N-deps-foreground | M TestAcquireRefusesMissingDependencies BG + TestAcquireBackgroundNilBrokerWithSpawnRefuses / N-deps-background | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 |\n199|| session (acquire.go:225, argv.go:20) | M entry arm TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession / N-session-entry; spawn-site arm U3 shadowed (entry refuses first; measured at ARG) | U2 background never reads SessionID | U1 | U1 | M spawn-site arm TestBuildArgvRefusesMalformedSession / N-argv-session | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 |\n200|| commit (runtime_unix.go:35) | M wiring + widened member TestAcquireForegroundStagesCommitPhaseCustodyRefusal + TestAcquireCreatesRuntimeDirIdempotently / N-acquire-commit-refusal + non-directory leaf TestAcquireForegroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf / N-containment-odirectory-commit (remaining members pinned at ENS over shared commit code) | U2 background verifies, never ensures | M commit tests / N-mode-create, N-mode-narrower-create, N-fchmod-umask, N-ownership-uid, N-containment-mismatch, N-containment-symlink, N-containment-odirectory-commit, N-root-symlink-commit, N-root-wiring, N-root-missing-classify, N-commit-eacces-as-exist | U2 Verify never commits | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 |\n201|| verify (runtime_unix.go:106) | U2 foreground ensures; Ensure never calls Verify | M BG custody tests (mode, ownership, non-dir, symlink leaf/root, mismatch, absence, missing root) / N-acquire-verify-refusal, N-absence-remap-ownership, N-containment-odirectory-verify, N-containment-symlink-verify, N-containment-mismatch, N-root-symlink-verify, N-verify-absence-detail, N-background-absence-remap, N-root-missing-classify | U2 Ensure never calls Verify | M verify tests / N-mode-verify, N-mode-narrower-verify, N-ownership-uid, N-containment-mismatch, N-containment-symlink-verify, N-containment-odirectory-verify, N-root-symlink-verify, N-verify-absence-detail, N-root-missing-classify | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 |\n202|| absence (acquire.go:184,258) | U2 Ensure creates; absence never surfaces on the creating path | M VerifiesWithoutCreating ×3 / N-background-absence-remap + N-verify-absence-detail; mode / N-absence-remap-widen; ownership / N-absence-remap-ownership; containment / N-absence-remap-containment; missing root / N-absence-remap-invalid | U2 | M TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesAbsence / N-verify-absence-detail (detail production; remap lives in Acquire) | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 |\n203|| creation (acquire.go:277) | U2 foreground creation allowed; path never consults the gate (deliberate, no dead call) | M miss tables 8 shapes + linux + wsl2 / N-creation-literal + D-background-fallback + D-background-fallback-foreground (24-test spy census arms both foreground dependencies) | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | M TestCheckCreationAllowedRefusesBackground / N-creation-literal |\n204|| broker (readiness.go:80) | U2 foreground decides the server admission directly, never a broker principal | M miss-table no-broker, foreign-user, generation-unbound / N-broker-uid + N-broker-generation (both-empty pair U3: details gate refuses empty Generation first) | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | M TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact / N-broker-uid + N-broker-generation + N-broker-empty-generation | U2 decides the server admission only, no principal | U2 |\n205|| broker-server (readiness.go:86) | U2 foreground never decides through a broker report | M miss-table server subtests ×5 / N-broker-zero-admission (R10/R19 members test-pinned, anchor shared — replay-verified) | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | M broker-contact server subtests ×5 / N-broker-zero-admission | U2 wiring lives in CheckBrokerContact; CheckServerAttested is downstream | U2 |\n206|| server (readiness.go:40) | M running tests ×4 / N-realm-membership + N-realm-generation + N-unattested-foreground (both-empty U3: details gate precedes) | M miss-table server subtests ×5 + catalog-decoy table / N-realm-membership + N-realm-generation + N-broker-zero-admission (admitted-without-gen test-pinned, R10 anchor shared — replay-verified; the 15 catalog decoys are test-pinned, row N-realm-membership keeps its headless_creation member) | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | M broker-contact server subtests ×5 / N-realm-membership + N-realm-generation (both-empty server pair U3: principal arm precedes) | M TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct ×6 + catalog-decoy table / N-realm-membership + N-realm-generation + N-realm-empty-want | U2 |\n207|| running (acquire.go:236) | M running tests + probe-failure / N-running-empty-admission + N-running-empty-generation + N-unattested-foreground | U2 background decides the broker report, never a Running flag | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 BRO/SRV decide admissions without a Running flag | U2 | U2 |\n208|| probe (acquire.go:190,232) | M TestAcquireForegroundProbeFailurePassesThrough / N-probe-swallow-foreground | M TestAcquireBackgroundProbeFailurePassesThrough / N-probe-swallow-background | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 |\n209|| spawn (acquire.go:246) | M TestAcquireForegroundSpawnFailureReportsWithoutFallback + TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry / N-spawn-swallow | U2 no spawn call on the background path (structural); no-fallback proof is the spy census + D rows at creation × ABG | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 |\n210|| argv (argv.go:17,24) | M TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer full element compare / N-argv-detached + N-argv-tail (socket/session arms U3: socket always derived, session pre-validated; CheckArgv shape arm B12: unreachable through Acquire) | U2 background never builds spawn argv | U2 | U2 | M exact-vector + ambient-socket + invalid-shape + malformed-session tests / N-argv-socket + N-argv-tmuxenv + N-argv-shape + N-argv-session + N-argv-detached + N-argv-tail | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 |\n211|\n212|SOCK (SocketPath) is a pure join and OBS (ObserveAmbient) records\n213|without deciding: neither enforces any gate, so their columns read U\n214|throughout by construction — the wiring gate pins what callers pass\n215|to the join. CRE decides only G-creation; every other CRE cell is U\n216|because the direct entry answers only \"may this caller create\" for\n217|post-gate caller values.\n218|\n219|## Stated bounds\n220|\n221|- B1 Determinism: no row has a real-tmux witness. Every broker, server,\n222|  and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies; the suite\n223|  passes with no tmux process anywhere. A live-server test would add a\n224|  witness, not a rule, and is sibling scope.\n225|- B2 Windows refusal: native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux (pinned SPEC\n226|  1458). The Windows platform refuses at the lexical gate on every host\n227|  (row 15); the Windows commit/verify arms refuse every platform and\n228|  exist only so the package compiles under GOOS=windows.\n229|- B3 Nil-dependency weakening on the foreground path panics instead of\n230|  misbehaving; the narrowing row pins the refusal and discloses the\n231|  panic kill.\n232|- B4 No gate inspects source text, so no token-preserving mutant\n233|  applies; the harness executes the behavioral suite.\n234|- B5 Attach presentation vectors are sibling scope: attached and broker\n235|  outcomes carry the socket, and only the spawned outcome carries argv.\n236|- B6 Lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, stop,\n237|  terminate, restore) belong to the sibling leaves, not to acquisition.\n238|- B7 The handle-mismatch arm stages its race through the sameDirectory\n239|  seam; a true concurrent handle swap is not staged.\n240|- B8 Registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the story's\n241|  final leaf; this leaf documents clause coverage here and in the\n242|  conformance matrix only.\n243|- B9 Adapter split: this leaf ships the decision core and argv only. No\n244|  production probe or spawner implementation exists in the tree; the\n245|  exec/probe adapters that report Reconcile/ResolveEvidence verdicts\n246|  and spawn through the built argv, and the server socket's crash\n247|  evidence, are owned by the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz. The\n248|  no-fallback proof covers spawns routed through Dependencies.Spawn;\n249|  a fallback through a direct os/exec call is excluded today only by\n250|  the import census (no os/exec import in the package).\n251|  Dependencies.Spawn is inert on the background path: a nil spawner\n252|  with a live broker still contacts (the broker path never calls it),\n253|  so the field is dead weight there — which is what makes the\n254|  shared-Dependencies fallback shape realistic, and why the spy\n255|  census arms the foreground probe alongside the spawner.\n256|- B10 Crash convergence assumes a umask that preserves owner rwx\n257|  (umask & 0700 == 0). Under an owner-bit-stripping umask a leaf\n258|  stranded between mkdirat and the explicit chmod refuses on retry\n259|  instead of converging, because existing leaves verify, never repair.\n260|- B11 A symlinked intermediate component inside the root path is\n261|  followed; only the root's last component refuses (row 9). This\n262|  matches the landed secprim root open and is the same bound.\n263|- B12 The landed argv shape refusal (BuildArgv via secprim.CheckArgv)\n264|  is reachable only by direct call with a non-filesystem runtime dir\n265|  (witnessed by TestBuildArgvRefusesInvalidArgvShape); through Acquire\n266|  the directory always names a created directory.\n267|- B13 Sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature verification, liveness,\n268|  and expiry are the landed Reconcile admission's verdict, consumed\n269|  here through Has. This leaf decides membership plus generation\n270|  binding only; the host-binding and provider-build cross-bind the\n271|  wrapper evaluates stays with the lifecycle owner.\n272|- B14 The battery and the read-only-root test assume a non-root test\n273|  user: N-fchmod-umask admits non-root creates past the explicit\n274|  chmod, so under root it is equivalent to the original and survives,\n275|  and TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesReadOnlyRoot stages a genuine EACCES\n276|  only when permission bits bind the test user. The reviewer's\n277|  same-shaped plant carries the identical assumption.\n278|- B15 Unmeasured fail-closed stat arms, no seam: handleBoundToPath's\n279|  two stat-failure arms (runtime.go) and verifyOwnership's !ok arm\n280|  (ownership_unix.go) fail closed by code and are prose only by test —\n281|  no test can stage a Stat failure on an open directory handle, or a\n282|  stat without ownership metadata on unix, without a seam. The\n283|  guard.Resolve refusal arm (runtime.go) is unreachable through the\n284|  name grammar: every input the guard would refuse is refused earlier\n285|  by scalar, so the fail-open plant survives by construction. The\n286|  secprim.NewGuard refusal arm (runtime.go:94-96) is the same class:\n287|  no committed input reaches it. The same unstageable class covers\n288|  the commit-side Fchmod and parent-Fsync failure arms and the\n289|  commit-side (runtime_unix.go:76-79) and verify-side leaf-Stat\n290|  failure arms: no committed test stages those failures. An\n291|  unopenable (0000) root reports `runtime containment` on both entries\n292|  with no committed test staging it — classifying EACCES as missing\n293|  would reroute it to `runtime root`, refusal-to-refusal. Reported\n294|  as error-arm rows, never counted among the narrowing survivors.\n295|- B16 The collision gate compares cleaned byte strings: an ambient\n296|  value naming the derived socket through a symlinked or relative\n297|  alias of the root walks past it (realpath equivalence is not\n298|  applied, and a cwd-relative spelling never equals the absolute\n299|  derived socket). Roots containing a comma are outside the TMUX\n300|  member's encoding: the gate splits at the first comma exactly as\n301|  tmux(1) itself does, so a comma-root socket component walks past\n302|  it. The spec rule is unaffected — the socket is derived, never\n303|  selected from an ambient value — so this bounds only the\n304|  package-local defense-in-depth claim. An `ax` invocation from\n305|  inside its own AX pane refuses `ambient collision` when the caller\n306|  populates Ambient from the process environment\n307|  (TMUX=`<derived>`,pid,idx in the real encoding): over-strict\n308|  rather than over-permissive, and the caller owns what it observes\n309|  — the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz decides the\n310|  nested-invocation rule deliberately.\n311|- B17 The mode gate reads permission bits only: setgid/sticky bits on\n312|  a 0700 leaf are admitted and macOS ACLs are not inspected. This\n313|  matches the landed hosttrust custody precedent\n314|  (internal/hosttrust/custody_unix.go platformModeOK: Perm() == mode),\n315|  so it is the same bound, not a fork.\n316|- B18 The derived socket path is not checked against the platform\n317|  sun_path limit (104 bytes on macOS); a deep runtime root surfaces\n318|  as a spawn failure in the lifecycle leaf's adapter, owned by\n319|  TASK-260830-1c28dz.\n320|- B19 The Runtime IPC root's own mode and ownership are not gated in\n321|  this leaf: the root arrives as the caller-supplied\n322|  localstore-resolved PathRuntime value, its creation-time custody is\n323|  the localstore layout owner's, and the SPEC 810-812\n324|  before-bind/connect rejection of an unsafe path, parent, or ancestor\n325|  is the lifecycle bind step's (TASK-260830-1c28dz), which is the step\n326|  that binds. This leaf pins the root handle (no-follow open plus\n327|  handle/path binding) and commits the leaf relative to it; a\n328|  world-writable root is admitted here and refused at bind. That the\n329|  root value is the landed localstore PathRuntime is a contract\n330|  statement about the caller, not a driven fact: no test composes\n331|  localstore with Acquire.\n332|- B20 Whether the runtime leaf was created by AX is indistinguishable\n333|  after the fact: any same-user 0700 directory under an admitted name\n334|  is accepted. The verifiable properties — mode, ownership, kind,\n335|  containment — are gated (rows 1-15); provenance is not claimed.\n336|- B21 No broker is modelled as the zero BrokerReport, whose\n337|  Principal.UID is 0: for a non-root process the absent broker\n338|  refuses on the authentication arm, while under a root process the\n339|  same-user arm passes and refusal comes from the generation arm.\n340|  The broker-path outcome socket binding is the generation equality\n341|  only — BrokerReport carries no socket of its own.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
