{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-000000011d7b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c620-a10f-77d2-842c-eaf24fab8e2e"},"sequence":11544,"recorded_at":1780531400023083,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0cdc816d-6145-48a9-a49c-390655512ae9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0cdc816d-6145-48a9-a49c-390655512ae9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0cdc816d-6145-48a9-a49c-390655512ae9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c6b0-1471-7c22-b37c-74d534e4d822"},"task_id":"01a0c6b0-1471-7c22-b37c-74d534e4d822","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c6b0-1471-7c22-b37c-74d534e4d822","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-348-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -40 LOGBOOK.md; echo ...; grep -n \\\"TASK-260830-35urbp\\\\|tmuxserver\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head\",\n  \"description\": \"Check LOGBOOK format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-21\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev7 — Commit-side O_DIRECTORY pin, WSL2 miss member, catalog-derived decoy completeness\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev6 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, one P2, two P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev5 finding stays closed with its driven evidence kept — production behaved correctly at every point the review drove, and this revision ships no production change). The census counts reproduce mechanically (24 × 11 = 264 cells; 50 measured / 4 bounds / 210 unreachable) with per-entry kill attribution holding for all 50 measured cells.\\n- P2-A (commit-side O_DIRECTORY arm without a narrowing row): the commit side gets the verify side's fixtures — a 0700 regular-file leaf on `EnsureRuntimeDir` (admit direction) and through foreground `Acquire` (no probe, no spawn), plus a FIFO leaf on `EnsureRuntimeDir` under the shared `verifyWithDeadline` (no-hang) — and shipped row `N-containment-odirectory-commit`, named under row 5 and in the `commit × ENS` / `commit × AFG` census cells; the `N-containment-odirectory-verify` note now points at the commit row instead of asserting it. Under the plant the 0700 leaf is admitted on `Ensure` and through the entry (which probes once and spawns once into `<root>/tmux/ax.sock`) while the FIFO blocks the full 5s.\\n- P3-A (no-fallback miss arm pinned for macOS/Linux only): the Linux miss test is a platform table `{linux, wsl2}`, so `N-creation-literal` and both D rows kill through all three tmux platforms; the WSL2-guarded fallback shape now reddens on the wsl2 member only. P3-B (attestation membership pinned for one decoy of sixteen): the decoy set is derived from `catalog.Current().Capabilities` (Section 4.D, sixteen-value table asserted), every non-realm member alone and all fifteen together refuse at `CheckServerAttested` and through the background miss; `N-realm-membership` keeps its `headless_creation` member with its mask extended to the new tables. Both-spy census is 24/24 by mechanical recount.\\n- Two-sided-gate symmetry check (new instrument run against the census): every gate implemented on two or more sides compared side by side — mode 2/2, O_DIRECTORY 1/1, symlink leaf 1/1, root no-follow 1/1, session 1/1, dispatch 1/1, deps 1/1, probe 1/1, custody wiring 1/1, leaf wiring 1/1/1, details 3/3 members, absence classifier 5/5 members — all symmetric; the O_DIRECTORY commit side was the one this round closed. Optional observations taken: crash-child output captured, `TestBuildArgvRefusesInvalidArgvShape` named under B12, matrix row-46 de-duplicated, `N-details-constructor` note corrected to the typed-nil mechanism.\\n- Battery: 73 narrowing + 2 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 76/76 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 58 of 58 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev7). Full 30-command suite green firsthand; `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev6 — Gate × entry census instrument + broker-wiring, ownership, and session-entry pins\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev5 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, one P2 class with four measured members, two P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev4 finding stays closed with its driven evidence kept — production behaved correctly at every point the review drove). The deliverable this round is the instrument: a gate × entry census (24 gates × 11 entries = 264 cells: 50 measured with a named test plus an admitting narrowing row each, 4 stated bounds, 210 unreachable with structural reasons) in TRACEABILITY.md, mirrored in the conformance matrix. Building it surfaced and closed member gaps beyond the four the reviewer measured.\\n- P2-A (broker-or-refuse pinned at the entry only for fixture shapes): three server-admission subtests (zero admission, admitted-without-generation, decoy-only) added to `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` AND mirrored in `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`; shipped `N-broker-zero-admission` at the `CheckBrokerContact` server wiring (R09 shape; R10/R19 share the anchor — replay-verified killed by the new tests); a fail-if-called `ProbeServer` spy armed in every background-path `Acquire` test (23/23 mechanical census, incl. the miss tables and `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating`); shipped `D-background-fallback-foreground` (R18 shape: fallback into `acquireForeground` guarded on `ProbeServer`) with the row-31/README sentence extended to both foreground dependencies.\\n- P3-A (ownership member of the absence class): new `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` (unix-only file, `effectiveUID` seam) asserting the top-level `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime ownership` with no broker contact and both spies silent, plus shipped `N-absence-remap-ownership` (R01 shape); the census added the sibling rows `N-absence-remap-containment` and `N-absence-remap-invalid` so every classifier member carries a row. P3-B (false \\\"before any side effect\\\"): session identity now parses at the foreground entry before `EnsureRuntimeDir` and the probe, with no-directory/no-probe assertions in `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession` and shipped `N-session-entry` (kills through the side-effect assertions while the refusal code stays correct).\\n- Census-driven closures beyond the verdict: caller-dimension subtests on the pre-dispatch gates (override/collision/details/unknown-platform tables drive both callers); `N-dispatch-foreground`/`N-dispatch-background` for the caller→path routing; `N-wiring-lexical/ensure/verify` for the three `RuntimeDirName` sites; `N-details-generation/brokerstate/constructor` (incl. the input-reachable invalid-UTF-8 arm, pinned with a probe-order assertion); `N-root-symlink-commit/verify` plus verify- and background-entry symlink-root tests; `N-argv-detached/tail` with a full element-by-element vector assertion through the spawn entry; background-entry symlink-leaf and handle-mismatch tests; mask extensions so shared-site rows kill through every entry they cover (attribution verified per entry from the raw logs).\\n- Observations: row 23/B16 scope comma roots out of the TMUX member's encoding and symlinked-or-relative aliases out of the cleaned-string gate; B9 states `Dependencies.Spawn` as inert on the background path; B15 names the commit-side leaf-`Stat` and `NewGuard` arms; static-gate exit codes recorded in the evidence archive.\\n- Battery: 72 narrowing + 2 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 75/75 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 58 of 58 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev6). Full 30-command suite green firsthand (race gate in 6 bounded groups with identical flags, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev5 — Private tmux server management rework (custody oracle, Request.Name removal, platform-axis absence pin, spy census)\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev4 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, two P2, two P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev3 finding stays closed with its driven evidence kept — production behaved correctly at every point the review drove). P2-A: `requireLocalError` now asserts the TOP-LEVEL `*Error` (plus no reachable `*axerror.Error`), because `errors.As` looked through the `capability_unavailable` wrapper whose cause is redacted off the wire — the new `N-absence-remap-widen` (the reviewer's R05 shape: `runtimeAbsent` admitting `runtime mode`) SURVIVES under the old helper and KILLS under the fixed one, proven by replay; `N-background-absence-remap` kept for the other direction. Re-ran every custody row after the oracle change: none only passed because of the old helper.\\n- P2-B: `Request.Name` is DELETED — the acquisition entry always passes `RuntimeDirName`, so the outcome socket is `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths with no per-call spelling that can re-open the `§3.2` divergence (the reviewer's P01 probe is unstageable: the field does not exist; R11 is inapplicable). `TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath` asserts the literal `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` through `Acquire` for foreground and background, named under rows 16/56. P3-A: `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` now drives macos/linux/wsl2 subtests (the reviewer's R14 shape fails on linux+wsl2 firsthand, named under row 52). P3-B: the four unarmed background tests now arm the spy, and the README/`acquire.go` sentence is scoped to background-path `Acquire` tests — mechanical census: 12/12 armed.\\n- Observations: row 6 states the ELOOP darwin-equivalence (reasoned, not run); B15 gains the unopenable-root arm and the `Fchmod`/`Fsync`/leaf-`Stat` arms; B16 states the nested-invocation over-strict refusal (owner: TASK-260830-1c28dz); row 23 scopes the live collision members to `TMUXEnv`/`InheritedSocket`; B19 states the `localstore`-root caller contract as undriven.\\n- Battery: 55 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 57/57 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 58 of 58 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev5). Full 30-command suite green firsthand (race in bounded groups, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev4 — Private tmux server management rework (spec socket path, background absence code, Running-arm entry pins, TMUX encoding, bounds)\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev3 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, three P2, five P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev2 finding stays closed with its driven evidence kept). P2-A: the derived path is now the path the spec mandates — `RuntimeDirName = \\\"tmux\\\"`, `SocketName = \\\"ax.sock\\\"`, both asserted as spec literals plus the joined `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` in `TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir`; `Request.Root` is documented as the Runtime IPC root resolved by the landed `localstore` layout as `PathRuntime` (no second resolution), with a §3.2 row 56 in TRACEABILITY and the matrix. P2-B+P3-B: the verify side distinguishes `ENOENT` (new `runtime absent` detail) from `ENOTDIR`/`ELOOP`/other, the missing-root code is aligned across commit and verify through one shared classifier, and the background path maps an absent leaf to the typed `capability_unavailable` with no probe, no spawn, and no directory write — while an existing-but-unsafe leaf keeps its custody code (`TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` rewritten, `TestAcquireBackgroundMissingRootRefusesInvalid` added, narrowings `N-verify-absence-detail` / `N-background-absence-remap` / `N-root-missing-cla