{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-000000011da7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c620-a10f-77d2-842c-eaf24fab8e2e"},"sequence":11566,"recorded_at":1780531400023127,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0cdc816d-6145-48a9-a49c-390655512ae9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0cdc816d-6145-48a9-a49c-390655512ae9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0cdc816d-6145-48a9-a49c-390655512ae9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c6b0-3fee-7442-9798-f94cda9dd565"},"task_id":"01a0c6b0-3fee-7442-9798-f94cda9dd565","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c6b0-3fee-7442-9798-f94cda9dd565","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-6\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-21\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-22\n+\n+### TASK-260830-1c28dz — tmux lifecycle operations via structured commands (initial producer delivery)\n+\n+- SHIPPED the second `tmuxserver` leaf: `Execute` admits exactly the eight lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop, stale termination, restore) and refuses unknown ones; the exec adapter reconstructs the exact `tmux -S <socket> <subcommand>` vector per operation (forged binaries, flag injection, ambient discovery all refuse); the probed socket generation binds before execution (B18-B20); bodies are pure argv builders with the stable `ax pane SESSION_ID` entrypoint; effects run through the landed terminstance engine with strict per-operation deadlines, generation rechecks, and AX-side state memory, while attach/terminate/restore mirror the landed backend/fencing/axpane gates. Every mutating operation replays idempotently; uncertain receipts reconcile through status before resuming.\n+- Battery: 173 narrowing + 2 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED (100 new second-leaf narrowing rows with per-arm killers; first leaf's 76 rows still green, shared control). AC: 33 of 33 rows (59-91) driven through production entries by named tests. Second-leaf census: Table B 24×21 (10 measured), Table C 90×11 (all unreachable), Table D 90×21 (108 measured), every measured cell with a named test plus an admitting narrowing row; singleton arms bound by B22, engine-normalized status by B23.\n+- Full 30-command suite green firsthand on the frozen tree (gofmt, build, vet, full suite, race gate, cover, all fuzz gates, tracecheck, cataloggen, linux/windows builds, JSON check, board validate, diff check, windows vet); OUTCOME-keyed base-vs-candidate importer comparison clean (base 82 PASS retained, zero regressions). Evidence tarball with raw per-plant logs attached to `TASK-260830-1c28dz`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n+- Process note: a full-suite cover gate failed while the mutant harness was still running in the same tree — the cover run compiled against a planted mutant. Re-ran clean after the harness exited 0. Never run `go test` concurrently with the harness in one worktree.\n+\n+## 2026-09-21\n","final_result":true}}}
