{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-000000012683","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c620-a10f-77d2-842c-eaf24fab8e2e"},"sequence":12700,"recorded_at":1780531400025395,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0cdc816d-6145-48a9-a49c-390655512ae9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0cdc816d-6145-48a9-a49c-390655512ae9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0cdc816d-6145-48a9-a49c-390655512ae9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c6c1-ff17-7053-b763-861f02453360"},"task_id":"01a0c6c1-ff17-7053-b763-861f02453360","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c6c1-ff17-7053-b763-861f02453360","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-389-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board m 'check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=1); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=2); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=3); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=4); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=5); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=6); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=7); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=8); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=9); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=10)' 2>&1 | tail -2\\ntask-board m 'check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=11); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=12); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=13); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=14); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=15); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=16); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=17); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=18); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=19); check_item(TASK-260830-1c28dz, item=20)' 2>&1 | tail -2\",\n  \"description\": \"Check all 20 checklist items\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"[{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":1,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Implement create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop, stale termination, and restore via structured commands\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":2,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":3,\\\"text\\\":\\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":4,\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate x entry census is committed as a table in the conformance matrix and mirrored in TRACEABILITY: every production entry that reaches each gate gets a named test plus an admitting narrowing row, or unreachable with a reason, or a stated bound with an owner; every gate implemented on two or more sides carries a row-count symmetry line\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":5,\\\"text\\\":\\\"The eight named operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop, stale termination, restore) are each driven through a production entry by a named committed test, with the n-of-8 ratio and the call site stated per operation\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":6,\\\"text\\\":\\\"The exec and probe adapters that TASK-260830-35urbp declared as this leaf bound (its Dependencies had no production implementation) exist and are driven, and the server socket gets crash and idempotency evidence or an explicit purity bound\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":7,\\\"text\\\":\\\"The bounds 35urbp handed over are each dispositioned: B18 sun_path 104-byte limit on the derived socket path, B16 nested invocation from inside an AX pane (ambient collision, decide deliberately), B19/B20 SPEC 810-812 before-bind rejection of an unsafe root at the bind step, and the rev7 P3-A fresh-decoy foreground attach wiring if attach semantics land here rather than in g0pcnt\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":8,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Composing packages keep working, proven by an OUTCOME-keyed comparison over the complete importer set (not a name-keyed per-test diff of one package), with every input that moved across an admission or refusal arm named in the results\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":9,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every rule is driven to its effect by a committed test that passes with NO tmux process anywhere; any real-tmux test is separately gated and is never the only witness for an acceptance row, and the results state which rows have a real-tmux witness in addition to their deterministic one\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":10,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\"}}]\\n[{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":11,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":12,\\\"text\\\":\\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft \\\\u003ccheckpoint_oid\\\\u003e` before completing again.\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":13,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":14,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":15,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":16,\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":17,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Lint clean\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":18,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":19,\\\"text\\\":\\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":20,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\"}}]\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5505,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1377,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
